            <ArticleTitle>Extraskeletal effects and manifestations of Vitamin D deficiency.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>602-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/2230-8210.113750</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The actions of vitamin D are not confined to bone. Vitamin D receptors are present in nearly all the nuclei and its actions are manifold. Populations deficient in vitamin D are at higher risk of developing autoimmune diseases, diabetes, cancer, infections, allergies and other chronic illnesses.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
